{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The proof repeatedly composes each induction hypothesis with trivial membership functions for list append. Using `List.append_subset.mpr` expresses those structural subset goals directly, reducing both proof syntax and elaboration work while preserving the special normalized-application contradiction case.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro Hnorm\\n  induction post <;>\\n    simp [Imperative.HasVarsPure.getVars, extractOldExprVars,\\n      Lambda.LExpr.LExpr.getVars] at * <;>\\n    try simp_all\\n  case app fn e fn_ih e_ih =>\\n    unfold extractOldExprVars\\n    split\\n    · simp [Lambda.LExpr.LExpr.getVars]\\n      intro x Hin\\n      exact Hin\\n    · next Hfalse =>\\n      cases Hnorm with\\n      | app Hfn He Hnold =>\\n        exfalso\\n        specialize Hnold (by constructor)\\n        cases Hnold\\n        exact Hfalse rfl\\n    · cases Hnorm with\\n      | app Hfn He _ =>\\n        apply List.append_subset.mpr\\n        exact ⟨fn_ih Hfn, e_ih He⟩\\n  case abs ih =>\\n    cases Hnorm\\n    apply ih <;> assumption\\n  case quant trih eih =>\\n    cases Hnorm\\n    apply List.append_subset.mpr\\n    constructor\\n    · apply trih <;> assumption\\n    · apply eih <;> assumption\\n  case ite cih tih eih =>\\n    cases Hnorm\\n    apply List.append_subset.mpr\\n    constructor\\n    · apply cih <;> assumption\\n    · apply List.append_subset.mpr\\n      constructor\\n      · apply tih <;> assumption\\n      · apply eih <;> assumption\\n  case eq ih1 ih2 =>\\n    cases Hnorm\\n    apply List.append_subset.mpr\\n    constructor\\n    · apply ih1 <;> assumption\\n    · apply ih2 <;> assumption\"}"}}
